{"name":"Smokehouse","hex":"#716354","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"smokehouse","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A structure used to smoke food to preserve it and to add flavor.","A structure in which freshly harvested tobacco is cured or preserved by smoking."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smokehouse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Smokehouse","blocks":[{"text":"A smokehouse or smokery (British) is a building where meat or fish is cured with smoke. The finished product might be stored in the building, sometimes for a year or more. Even when smoke is not used, such a building—typically a subsidiary building—is sometimes referred to as a \"smokehouse\". When smoke is not used, the term meathouse or meat house is common."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Reitman%27s_Smokehouse%3B_Campbell_County%2C_Kentucky.JPG/330px-Reitman%27s_Smokehouse%3B_Campbell_County%2C_Kentucky.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smokehouse","wikidata":"Q1442496"},{"title":"Smokehouse (story collection)","blocks":[{"text":"Smokehouse is a 2020 short story collection by the Australian author Melissa Manning."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/85/Smokehouse_%28story_collection%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smokehouse_(story_collection)","wikidata":"Q134008460"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Picswiss_BE-91-01_Freilichtmuseum_Ballenberg-.jpg/330px-Picswiss_BE-91-01_Freilichtmuseum_Ballenberg-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Picswiss_BE-91-01_Freilichtmuseum_Ballenberg-.jpg/330px-Picswiss_BE-91-01_Freilichtmuseum_Ballenberg-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse